**Added elements and why:**
- 1 added server: a second web server (Nginx). It serves traffic together with the first one, so the web tier is no longer a single server.
- Load balancers (HAProxy) configured as a cluster: a second load balancer takes over if the first fails, so the load balancer is no longer a SPOF.
- Components split onto their own servers: the web server, the application server and the database each run on their own server, so each can be scaled, secured and maintained on its own.

**Result:** load balancer cluster, 2 web servers, 1 application server, 1 database server.
